kitty leaves native fullscreen before destroying a window —
applies to v0.48.2 (2cb1d95c3a) with `git apply`, after kitty-upstream-defects.patch and
kitty-talk-thread-survives-v0.48.2.patch; kitty-upstream-backport-v0.48.2.patch applies after it.
(git apply ignores every line above the first diff header, so this block is commentary only.)

Why (2026-10-16, operator ruling on decision a41897063971): kitty 0.48.2 SIGSEGV'd on 2026-10-15 in
-[_NSExitFullScreenTransitionController dealloc] -> -[NSWindow dealloc] after it closed a
native-fullscreen OS window while the window was still in fullscreen; the repro showed every destroy
path does that (32/32). Evidence: docs/research/kitty-crash-2026-10-15/README.md.

Part 1, glfw/cocoa_window.m: _glfwPlatformDestroyWindow, when the window is in native fullscreen or
mid-transition, tears down the GLFW side as before but does not order out or close the NSWindow.
GLFWDeferredClose takes it (retained, plain content view, ignores mouse), leaves fullscreen through
-[GLFWWindow leaveFullScreenDetached] (super's toggleFullScreen:, since GLFWWindow's override
dereferences the now-NULL glfw_window), and closes it 0.3 s after windowDidExitFullScreen:, or at
once on a failed enter/exit; a 5 s timeout starts the exit itself once, then closes. canBecomeMainWindow
gains the NULL check canBecomeKeyWindow already had. Traditional fullscreen is unchanged.
2026-10-16, after upstream review: -[GLFWDeferredClose finish] skips the Tahoe zero-size frame while
the window still carries the fullscreen style mask (the timeout and failed-exit paths can reach it
before the exit finished), as upstream 7e88f51ed7 does in _glfwPlatformDestroyWindow. orderOut stays
unconditional, as it does there.

Part 2, kitty/rc/action.py (REMOVED 2026-10-16): the client sends the match as `match_window` (its
protocol spec), the server's windows_for_match_payload reads `match`, so `@ action --match` ran on
the active window and a non-matching spec never failed. One line re-keyed the payload; no match kept
the active-window default. Upstream fixed
the same bug in 0ea80af638 (kovidgoyal/kitty#10672) by letting windows_for_match_payload read
'match_window', which behaves the same; kitty-upstream-backport-v0.48.2.patch carries that fix now,
so this patch no longer touches kitty/rc.

Reported upstream: see the README section "Kitty patch and upstream reports (2026-10-16)".
Built by: scripts/kitty-build-swap.sh build --no-band (applies the four patches in order; this is
the third).

